  "answer": "**Every new session restores on demand; no pre-started or pre-restored V2 instances were seen.** 5/5 new V2 sessions restored the version's snapshot (sessions shared 2 snapshot copies per runtime), each restored at most 0.08 s before its first request arrived (5/5 \u22642 s), and before the first session nothing was booted or restored outside the snapshot build. V1, for comparison, does keep a warm pool: 5/5 V1 sessions landed on their own instance that had been booted ahead of time (median 4.7 min before the session, newest 4.5 min), ran ~3.3 s, was frozen, and was resumed ~0.13 s before the first request; 10 V1 instances had booted before the first session was even sent. At this low, sequential load that pool made V1's cold invoke (p50 511 ms) faster than V2's (p50 2.03 s)."
